{
  "tema": 6470,
  "slug": "pude-haber",
  "titulo": "Poder + haber + participle = could have done",
  "subtitulo": "Pudiste haberme avisado. Podríamos haber ido.",
  "foto": "t09.jpg",
  "regla": "Could have done = pude / podía / podría + haber + participle. All three mean the same: there was a chance, and it didn't happen.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "_Could have [done]_ is a missed chance in the past. Spanish has **three** forms, and they're interchangeable:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Form",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "preterite: pude + haber + participle",
              "Pudo haber ido."
            ],
            [
              "imperfect: podía + haber + participle",
              "Podía haber ido."
            ],
            [
              "conditional: podría + haber + participle",
              "Podría haber ido."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Only **poder** is conjugated. **Haber** stays in the infinitive, followed by the participle."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Pronouns go in front of **poder** or attached to **haber**: **me podrías haber avisado** = **podrías haberme avisado**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **poder** + **haber**: you were able to, but you didn't."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Gabriela ==pudo haber ido== a la UNAM, pero no fue.",
              "en": "Gabriela could have gone to UNAM, but she didn't."
            },
            {
              "es": "Gabriela ==podía haber ido== a la UNAM, pero no fue.",
              "en": "Gabriela could have gone to UNAM, but she didn't."
            },
            {
              "es": "Gabriela ==podría haber ido== a la UNAM, pero no fue.",
              "en": "Gabriela could have gone to UNAM, but she didn't."
            },
            {
              "es": "Me ==podrías haber avisado== para ir por ti a la central.",
              "en": "You could have told me, so I could pick you up at the bus station."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Pudimos haber ido== a la playa en lugar de a la sierra.",
              "en": "We could have gone to the beach instead of the mountains."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Podrían haber organizado== mejor el viaje; fue un desastre.",
              "en": "They could have planned the trip better; it was a disaster."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
